From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Nov 2026 00:53:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: sc2336p: name the likely SC2337P when the die does not match

Boards in this family ship either the SC2336P or the SC2337P, and the PT2
profile exists for both. The sc2336p driver rejects the SC2337P die with
only "chip found ... is not an sc2336p chip", so the user gets a dead
streamer and no hint. Add the chip id and the image to flash.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

diff --git a/3.10.14/sensor-src/t23/sc2336p.c b/3.10.14/sensor-src/t23/sc2336p.c
--- a/3.10.14/sensor-src/t23/sc2336p.c
+++ b/3.10.14/sensor-src/t23/sc2336p.c
@@ -1299,6 +1299,9 @@ static int sensor_g_chip_ident(struct tx_isp_subdev *sd, struct tx_isp_chip_ident *chip)
 	ret = sensor_detect(sd, &ident);
 	if (ret) {
-		ISP_ERROR("chip found @ 0x%x (%s) is not an %s chip.\n",
-			  client->addr, client->adapter->name, SENSOR_NAME);
+		ISP_ERROR("chip found @ 0x%x (%s) is not an %s chip (chip id 0x%04x).\n",
+			  client->addr, client->adapter->name, SENSOR_NAME, ident);
+		if (ident == 0x9b3a) {
+			ISP_ERROR("this looks like an SC2337P; flash the sc2337p image for this board.\n");
+		}
 		return ret;
 	}
